  -| D-07 | major | FIXED | `e4d9b1fd`, `92a68252`, `3539b9f6`, `854d267d`, `1145e839` | `cli/test/provider_status_plain.test.ts` describes "D-07: first run without a provider" (4), "D-07 review round 2" (12: /models 401 and 403 with working chat run the prompt, /models 503 or a timeout does not block, a real fetch timeout against a server that never answers is not a refusal, the refusal wording for TLS/reset says "could not connect", a steer, a deferred follow-up and `/image` on a dead provider are refused instead of run, a cancel during the gate is reported once and keeps the gate, a refused prompt is not in history, `scrubUrls` cuts every userinfo form and leaves other text alone, no URL credential in any rendered string) and "D-07 review follow-ups" (1: a prompt sent before the start-up probe ends is gated); Rust `live_state::tests::a_prompt_refused_for_want_of_a_provider_goes_back_to_the_composer_with_the_reason`, `a_refused_prompt_does_not_overwrite_what_was_typed_meanwhile`, `a_refused_prompt_with_a_paste_comes_back_as_the_paste_label_not_its_expansion`, `a_refused_prompt_keeps_the_recall_history_made_in_the_meantime`, `composer::tests::restoring_a_draft_brings_back_its_text_and_pastes_but_keeps_the_history_made_since`; `live_view::tests::a_first_run_without_a_provider_shows_the_next_step_at_every_width` (40/60/100 cols) | When start-up cannot connect (connection refused, DNS, TLS, reset) the notice says what is missing (`No model is connected: nothing answers at <endpoint>`), `/connect`, a local model server (LM Studio, Ollama, llama.cpp), `nexus doctor` and `docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`; the cause chain is in `/details`. Only that state gates: a prompt, a steer that would start a turn and a deferred follow-up all go through one `gatedTurn` that waits for the start-up probe, probes again (3 s, so a server started or `/connect` done since is honoured) and, if still down, refuses with the reason (`NO_PROVIDER` for a prompt; the steer acknowledgement `cancelled` with the text returned for steer and follow-up) instead of entering the retry loop; a refused message is not added to prompt history, and the TUI restores the draft (text, paste buffers, cursor; recall history untouched) when its composer is empty. Only a failed connection (refused, DNS, TLS, reset) gates, and a TLS or reset failure is worded "could not connect" rather than "nothing answers"; a timeout, an HTTP error from `/models` (503 while a model loads, 429) or a 401 or 403 is only a warning (`rejected the credentials on the start-up check; Nexus will still try your messages`): it never blocks, because the chat path refreshes tokens and may accept a key the model list refuses. New: error code `NO_PROVIDER` (older TUIs show `NO_PROVIDER: <message>` and do not restore the draft). Limitations: a `/` in a URL REDACTEDword defeats the credential scrub (it needs a rule for unparseable URLs); the scheme-less `user:REDACTED@host` form is cut only when a `/` follows the host; the scrub is O(n^2) on a long run without spaces (inputs are error messages capped well below that); `bad port` (a fetch-banned port) is worded "nothing answers"; `/tdd`, `/team` and `/compact --llm` call the model inside the command and are not gated; a cancel during the gate returns the message (`Cancelled before it was sent.`) or lets the turn report INTERRUPTED; the refusal says to use `/connect`, which saves a credential but only a model selection rebuilds the client, so after `/connect` pick a model too; the TUI does not open the connect panel by itself (the notice names it); the header still shows the configured model name (the placeholder `local-model` when none); a provider that goes down after start-up is handled by the D-06 wait, not this refusal. Captures: `docs/evidence/v1.1.4/tui/D-07/` |
  +| D-07 | major | FIXED | `e4d9b1fd`, `92a68252`, `3539b9f6`, `854d267d`, `1145e839` | `cli/test/provider_status_plain.test.ts` describes "D-07: first run without a provider" (4), "D-07 review round 2" (12: /models 401 and 403 with working chat run the prompt, /models 503 or a timeout does not block, a real fetch timeout against a server that never answers is not a refusal, the refusal wording for TLS/reset says "could not connect", a steer, a deferred follow-up and `/image` on a dead provider are refused instead of run, a cancel during the gate is reported once and keeps the gate, a refused prompt is not in history, `scrubUrls` cuts every userinfo form and leaves other text alone, no URL credential in any rendered string) and "D-07 review follow-ups" (1: a prompt sent before the start-up probe ends is gated); Rust `live_state::tests::a_prompt_refused_for_want_of_a_provider_goes_back_to_the_composer_with_the_reason`, `a_refused_prompt_does_not_overwrite_what_was_typed_meanwhile`, `a_refused_prompt_with_a_paste_comes_back_as_the_paste_label_not_its_expansion`, `a_refused_prompt_keeps_the_recall_history_made_in_the_meantime`, `composer::tests::restoring_a_draft_brings_back_its_text_and_pastes_but_keeps_the_history_made_since`; `live_view::tests::a_first_run_without_a_provider_shows_the_next_step_at_every_width` (40/60/100 cols) | When start-up cannot connect (connection refused, DNS, TLS, reset) the notice says what is missing (`No model is connected: nothing answers at <endpoint>` for a refused connection or an unresolvable host, read from the transport's error code; `could not connect to <endpoint>` for TLS, reset and anything else), `/connect`, a local model server (LM Studio, Ollama, llama.cpp), `nexus doctor` and `docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`; the cause chain is in `/details`. Only that state gates: a prompt, a steer that would start a turn and a deferred follow-up all go through one `gatedTurn` that waits for the start-up probe, probes again (3 s, so a server started or `/connect` done since is honoured) and, if still down, refuses with the reason (`NO_PROVIDER` for a prompt; the steer acknowledgement `cancelled` with the text returned for steer and follow-up) instead of entering the retry loop; a refused message is not added to prompt history, and the TUI restores the draft (text, paste buffers, cursor; recall history untouched) when its composer is empty. Only a failed connection (refused, DNS, TLS, reset) gates, and a TLS or reset failure is worded "could not connect" rather than "nothing answers"; a timeout, an HTTP error from `/models` (503 while a model loads, 429) or a 401 or 403 is only a warning (`rejected the credentials on the start-up check; Nexus will still try your messages`): it never blocks, because the chat path refreshes tokens and may accept a key the model list refuses. New: error code `NO_PROVIDER` (older TUIs show `NO_PROVIDER: <message>` and do not restore the draft). Limitations: the credential scrub now cuts a REDACTEDword holding a raw `/` (`https://u:abc/def@host/v1`), and still does not cut an all-digit REDACTEDword (`u:1234/x@h` reads as a port), a REDACTEDword-less `TOKEN@host/x` scheme-less, or `user:REDACTED@host:port` with no trailing `/`; the scrub is O(n^2) on a long run without spaces (inputs are error messages capped well below that); the first scrub rule can over-cut diagnostic text when `//host:port` is followed on the same line by a later `@`; `/tdd`, `/team` and `/compact --llm` call the model inside the command and are not gated; a cancel during the gate returns the message (`Cancelled before it was sent.`) or lets the turn report INTERRUPTED; the refusal says to use `/connect`, which saves a credential but only a model selection rebuilds the client, so after `/connect` pick a model too; the TUI does not open the connect panel by itself (the notice names it); the header still shows the configured model name (the placeholder `local-model` when none); a provider that goes down after start-up is handled by the D-06 wait, not this refusal. Captures: `docs/evidence/v1.1.4/tui/D-07/` |
  +1 -1

